Company Name: RED POWER LIMITED T/A RED POWER MOTORSPORT 
Job Location: UNIT 1B &amp; 1C AVONBEG INDUSTRIAL ESTATE LONG MILE ROAD DUBLIN 12 D12 HE02

We are looking for an Car Mechanic to join our team, responsible for carrying out inspections, repairs and maintenance on motor vehicles, ensuring safety, quality and efficiency in the services provided.

Responsibilities
Visually checks, test drives or uses test equipment to diagnose engine and mechanical faults;
Removes, dismantles, repairs and replaces defective parts and prepares new parts using appropriate tools;
Reassembles, tests, adjusts and tunes the appropriate parts, systems or entire engine;
Carries out routine maintenance checks on oil and air filters, brakes and other vehicle parts/systems;
Diagnoses faults in electrical/electronic circuitry, removes faulty components and fits replacements;
Checks condition of electrical/electronic systems and carries out servicing tasks;
Installs additional electrical amenities;
Repairs and services air conditioning, heating and engine-cooling systems.

Requirements
No formal academic qualification required;
Previous experience in automotive mechanics will be considered an advantage;
Ability to work in a team and strong attention to detail;
Willingness to learn and continuously improve.

Annual Salary: €36.605
Hours Salary: €18.05
Weekly Hours: 39 hours
Start Date: 07/12/2026
Company Contact:
 Email: sunni@redpowermotorsport.ie

In order to work in Ireland a non-EEA National, unless they are exempted, must hold a valid employment permit.  Please review the Eligibility and requirements for an employment permit if you are unsure of your eligibility to apply for this vacancy. <br>  Job Title: Playgroup Leader
Company Name: Migra Br Limited
Work Location: 6 Fern Road, Sandy Ford Business Park, Dublin 18 D18FP98

Job Description:
We are looking for a dedicated and enthusiastic Playgroup Leader to deliver and facilitate play opportunities for children in a safe and stimulating environment. The role involves supporting pre-school children in both structured and informal settings, promoting independence, confidence and social interaction.

Key Responsibilities
Supervise children’s games and encourage the development of physical, social and language skills;
Provide play areas and prepare materials for a wide range of children’s activities;
Encourage children’s independence, self-confidence and social interaction;
Organise and supervise children on excursions;
Organise and supervise activities in accordance with Health and Safety regulations, responding appropriately to injuries and emergencies;
Put away equipment and clean premises after use;
Liaise with parents, carers and colleagues, maintaining appropriate records.

Requirements
1–2 years’ experience in early childhood education or recreation roles is desirable;
Strong leadership and organisational skills in managing groups of children;
Passion for working with children, excellent communication and a positive attitude

Annual Salary: € 36605 annual - € 18.05
Hours per Week: 39
Start Date: 14/12/2026

Company Contact: Danusa Migra br

